---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Points Program | IEEE NMSU Student Chapter"
    description="How IEEE NMSU Student Chapter members earn points toward the Rising Stars Conference delegation, plus ready-to-use spreadsheet templates."
    ogTitle="Points Program | IEEE NMSU Student Chapter"
    ogDescription="How members earn points toward the Rising Stars Conference delegation."
    noindex
>
<main id="main">
        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="section-head reveal in">
                    <span class="section-index">IEEE</span>
                    <h1 class="section-title">NMSU Student Chapter Points Program</h1>
                </div>
                <p class="section-sub reveal in">How members earn points toward a seat at the IEEE Rising Stars Conference, and the spreadsheet templates used to track it all.</p>

                <div class="panel reveal">
                    <h2>Ways to earn points</h2>
                    <table class="points-table">
                        <thead>
                            <tr><th>Activity</th><th>Points</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr><td>Attend an IEEE chapter meeting</td><td>10 pts</td><td>Logged from the meeting sign-in sheet</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Table at a chapter event</td><td>5 pts</td><td>Recruiting tables, outreach, career fair shifts</td></tr>
                            <tr><td>Complete an alumni brick</td><td>5 pts</td><td>See the Legacy Brick Project below</td></tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="panel reveal">
                    <h2>Rising Stars Conference selection</h2>
                    <ul class="step-list">
                        <li>All current chapter officers attend the IEEE Rising Stars Conference.</li>
                        <li>The <strong>2 non-officer members with the highest point totals</strong> for the semester earn a seat alongside them.</li>
                        <li>Standings reset at the start of each semester, so every member starts even.</li>
                        <li>Ties are broken by number of bricks completed, then by earliest chapter join date.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="panel reveal">
                    <h2>The Legacy Brick Project</h2>
                    <p class="section-sub" style="margin-bottom: 1.2rem;">The chapter salvaged the bricks from Thomas &amp; Brown, the old ECE building, before it was demolished. A gift of $500 to the chapter is recognized with one of them, engraved and shipped to the donor. The bricks are not sold; they are a thank-you to the donor. Members earn points by taking a brick from claim to finished product.</p>
                    <p style="margin: 0 0 1.2rem;"><a class="btn" href="/ieee-bricks.html">Alumni-facing page &rarr;</a></p>
                    <ol class="step-list">
                        <li>An alum gives $500 to the chapter and is added to the Brick Claims sheet as <strong>Unclaimed</strong>.</li>
                        <li>A student claims an open brick by adding their name to the sheet.</li>
                        <li>The student edits the chapter's brick template file with the alum's name.</li>
                        <li>The student takes the file to the machine shop to have it engraved.</li>
                        <li>The student submits a photo of the finished brick. Once verified, 5 points are logged and the brick is marked <strong>Complete</strong>.</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="container">
                <div class="section-head reveal">
                    <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: 1.3rem;">Spreadsheet templates</h2>
                </div>
                <p class="section-sub">Download each CSV and import it into its own tab in a Google Sheet named something like "IEEE NMSU Chapter Points Tracker."</p>

                <div class="template-grid">
                    <div class="panel template-card reveal">
                        <h3>Officers</h3>
                        <p>Current officer roster, used to exclude officers from the top-2 eligibility check.</p>
                        <a class="btn" href="ieee-points-templates/officers.csv" download>Download CSV</a>
                    </div>
                    <div class="panel template-card reveal" data-delay="1">
                        <h3>Points Log</h3>
                        <p>One row per point-earning action: date, member, category, points, and proof.</p>
                        <a class="btn" href="ieee-points-templates/points-log.csv" download>Download CSV</a>
                    </div>
                    <div class="panel template-card reveal" data-delay="2">
                        <h3>Brick Claims</h3>
                        <p>Tracks every alumni brick order from claim through engraving to completion.</p>
                        <a class="btn" href="ieee-points-templates/brick-claims.csv" download>Download CSV</a>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="panel reveal">
                    <h2>Setting up the Standings tab</h2>
                    <p class="section-sub" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">After importing the three sheets above, add a fourth tab named <strong>Standings</strong> and list your current members in column A. These two formulas do the rest:</p>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        B2: =IF(COUNTIF(Officers!$A$2:$A,A2)&gt;0,"Yes","No")<br>
                        C2: =SUMIF('Points Log'!$B:$B,A2,'Points Log'!$D:$D)
                    </div>
                    <p class="section-sub" style="margin: 1rem 0 0;">Sort the tab by column C (Total Points) descending, then read down past anyone marked "Yes" in column B. The first two "No" rows are your Rising Stars invitees.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>
